# ...but the add-on manifest is source.
!nvda-addon/manifest.ini

# OpenTV: the original Centigram distribution, generated analysis output,
# build products and reference audio.  The distribution and the
# disassembly stay out; the engine's constant tables under data/ are
# deliberately committed instead, so a build needs no Centigram binary.
# See NOTICE for whose work those are.
/TruVoice/
/work/
/build/
/ref/
*.wav

# Copies of the Centigram demo texts that sit in the repository root
/ADDRBOOK.TXT
/ADDRESS.TXT
/HOMOGRPH.TXT
/PHONE.TXT
/SAMPLE.TXT

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc

/nvda/